 After a hard kill, `_eager_respawn(key)` calls `get_or_create(key)` in a background task so the next user message finds a warm session. On failure, logs at debug and does nothing — the next message triggers `get_or_create` again via the normal path.
 
+## Speculative Session Creation
+
+Dashboard `_eager_spawn` resolves agent bindings against `slot.project`, the
+same directory passed as the session's cwd. This applies to both fresh eager
+creation and resumed-session prefetch. Before resolving, it warms that project's
+agent index off the event loop through `warm_project_agent_names`; the resolver
+then runs inline against the warm cache, matching the real-turn path.
+
+Project-local `.kiro/agents/*.json` declarations remain dispatchable even when
+the gateway runs from an unrelated directory. Configured aliases retain their
+precedence, and the gateway's cwd never supplies an agent missing from the slot's
+project. Correct binding at prefetch time is required because the first real
+turn reuses the prefetched process, including its selected agent and hooks.
+
+On runtimes with app-agent self-healing, the retry after a materialized-agent
+refresh and the re-resolution after app registration retain that same project
+scope. Recovery must not replace the slot's project with an absent project.
+
